{
  "contract": "series",
  "version": 1,
  "description": "The chart lines: an instrument's AVCO cost line (computeCostBasisTimeline), its value against what is invested (computeInvestedVsValueSeries) and the portfolio's merge of those (computePortfolioInvestedVsValueSeries), with prices brought to euros first: each close at the last rate published on or before its own Madrid day and at most 7 days old (historyInBase), today's price at today's (pricesInBase); a close with no such rate is left out and counted in unrated. Instruments come in the order of their first trade, trades by instant, then BUY before SELL, then externalId, then id. A value series has one point per trade and per close at or after the first trade, plus today when there is a price, ordered by t; a trade comes before a close at the same t, and closes sharing a t keep the order given (history, then today). Each point is the last trade's invested and quantity times the point's price. The merge has one point per distinct t across instruments, each instrument contributing its last point at or before that t and nothing before its first. Shared with the mobile client: both implementations must reproduce every case. Events are LedgerEvents; an absent fxSource is IDENTITY and an absent funding is CASH. expect is written by running the TypeScript core; byHand.figures, where a case has it, are worked out by hand, its arithmetic says how, and each key is a dotted path into expect.",
